export default "Sleep can be hard to explain in a short visit. You may remember the worst night and forget the pattern.\n\nThis log puts sleep notes next to cycle notes. It covers trouble falling asleep, wake-ups, night sweats, and hot flashes in one place. It does not tell you the cause. It does not give sleep treatment advice.\n\nIt is not medical advice.\n\nIf safety is part of the issue, use your safety or crisis plan first. Do not wait to finish this sheet.\n\n## Start here\n\nFill this in before the daily log.\n\n| Field | Your notes |\n|---|---|\n| Date range | |\n| Last period start date | |\n| Usual cycle length, if known | |\n| Main sleep concern | falling asleep / staying asleep / early wake / night sweats / hot flashes |\n| Worst night so far | |\n| Main daytime problem | sleepy / foggy / mood / pain / work / care tasks |\n| Main question for care | |\n\nIf you do not know your cycle day, use plain timing. Try \"3 days before bleeding\" or \"period day 2.\"\n\n## Daily sleep and cycle log\n\nFill this out in the morning. Use the same time each day if you can.\n\n| Date | Cycle day | Period day | Bedtime | Wake time | Wake-ups | Sleep quality | Night sweats | Hot flashes | Daytime energy | Notes |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | | | | poor / okay / good | none / mild / soaked | none / mild / strong | low / medium / high | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n\nACOG lists insomnia and fatigue as possible PMS symptoms. The Office on Women's Health lists sleep problems, hot flashes, and night sweats as symptoms that may occur during the menopause transition. Your log can show timing. It does not name the cause.\n\n## Symptoms that showed up too\n\nCheck what fits.\n\n- [ ] Fatigue.\n- [ ] Low mood.\n- [ ] Anxiety.\n- [ ] Irritability.\n- [ ] Poor focus.\n- [ ] Headache.\n- [ ] Cramps or pelvic pain.\n- [ ] Breast pain.\n- [ ] Night sweats.\n- [ ] Hot flashes.\n- [ ] Food cravings.\n- [ ] Bleeding started or stopped.\n\n## Evening context\n\nNHLBI's sleep diary includes caffeine, alcohol, medicine notes, and daytime sleepiness. Use the same idea here.\n\n| Date | Caffeine time | Alcohol | Screen note | Stress note | Medicine change |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | none / morning / afternoon / evening | none / yes, amount | usual / late / more than usual | low / medium / high | name and date, if any |\n| | | | | | |\n| | | | | | |\n| | | | | | |\n\nDo not turn one row into a rule. Look for repeated timing.\n\n## Perimenopause context\n\nUse this table if periods are also changing, or if hot flashes and night sweats feel connected to a bigger shift.\n\n| Date | Cycle day, if known | Bleeding | Spotting | Period expected? | Sleep worse than usual? |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| | | none, light, medium, heavy | yes, no | yes, no, unsure | yes, no |\n| | | | | | |\n| | | | | | |\n\nIf you no longer bleed, write \"no bleeding\" or \"postmenopause.\" If bleeding starts after 12 months with no period or spotting, tell a clinician.\n\n## Daytime impact\n\nWrite what poor sleep changed.\n\n| Area | What changed? | How much? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Work or school | | none / some / a lot |\n| Care tasks | | none / some / a lot |\n| Focus | | none / some / a lot |\n| Mood | | none / some / a lot |\n| Driving or errands | | none / some / a lot |\n| Plans | | none / some / a lot |\n\n## Pattern check\n\nAnswer these after a week, after your period starts, or after a full cycle.\n\n| Question | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| How many nights were hard? | |\n| How many days before bleeding did it start? | |\n| Did sleep change once bleeding started? | |\n| Did night sweats or hot flashes happen too? | |\n| Did fatigue or mood change too? | |\n| Did this happen in past cycles? | |\n| Did it happen far from period timing too? | |\n| What do I want to ask? | |\n\nThe answer can be \"not sure.\" That still helps.\n\n## Questions for a clinician\n\nPick the questions that fit.\n\n- Could my cycle timing matter?\n- Could this fit a PMS or perimenopause pattern?\n- What other sleep causes should we check?\n- Should I keep a sleep diary for another cycle?\n- Which symptoms mean I should call sooner?\n- Should I bring a sleep summary instead of all notes?\n- What private details can I leave out?\n\nMedlinePlus suggests bringing questions and symptom notes to a visit. Keep your list short enough to use in the room.\n\n## One-page handoff\n\nCopy this into a note or print it.\n\n```text\nPeriod sleep visit summary\n\nDate range:\n\nLast period start date:\n\nSleep got worse:\n\nSleep got better:\n\nNight sweats or hot flashes:\n\nWorst sleep pattern:\n\nSymptoms near poor sleep:\n\nDaytime impact:\n\nQuestions:\n```\n\n## Privacy check before sharing\n\nSleep notes can include mood, sex, pregnancy worries, medicine names, conflict, location, work, and safety details.\n\nBefore you export, screenshot, print, email, or upload notes, ask:\n\n- Who needs this?\n- Do they need dates or the full log?\n- Can I share a summary instead?\n- Does it include private notes I can leave out?\n- Will it go into a portal?\n- Will it be saved in email or downloads?\n\nFloriva can keep sleep, period, and symptom notes together on your device. Paper works too. You choose what to type, export, screenshot, print, or share.\n\nFor storage choices, read the [sleep cycle data privacy checklist](/resources/privacy-in-practice/protect-your-symptom-and-condition-data). For visit prep, read [Floriva for gynecologist prep](/app-guides/floriva-for-gynecologist-prep).";
